      "message": "Good point, in general I like to have tracepoints which are consumable by their own, not sure if this is also a kind of requirement for mainline.\n\nHowever, it\u0027s true that in this case we quite likely always use this tracepoint in conjunction with others e.g. \"sched_wakeup\" and/or \"sched_switch\"... thus, what you propose makes sense to me. Probably we should to the same optimisation also for the many other tracepoints we have in the fastpath, namely:\n- sched_load_avg_task\n- sched_tune_tasks_update\n- sched_boost_task\n- sched_energy_diff\n- walt_update_task_ravg\n\nMaybe, since there are so many tracepoints \"duplicating\" the task name, it could make sense to merge this patch as is and add a dedicated patch on to which explicitly does this optimisation by removing the duplication in one go from all the above tracepoints. At least it would provide a consisted and documented update across the full set of scheduler tracepoints.\n\nWhat do you think?",
